# blue native (theory/BLUE-NATIVE.md): blue programs compiled to board images
# with no evaluator and no collector in them.
#
# A blue project of its own, lowered by the same engine as every project
# (nix/project.nix), from blue's flake (nix/native.nix, which adds the image
# and the QEMU check the Bluefile has no word for yet: `firmware` and `board`
# are milestone N1).
#
#   bidamas/kiban     board specs, and the host's model of a board's words
#   bidamas/chuuzou   the backend: a checked program to a typed Rust AST,
#                     emitted through tatara-rust-emit, linked, measured
#   seam/             the hand-written seam: kiban_io (safe) and one unsafe
#                     crate per board
#   programs/         the programs; images/ holds their emitted Rust
package("blue-native", "0.1.0")

packages("bidamas")

# The emitter chuuzou hands its typed Rust AST to (tatara-rust-ast's CLI).
tool("tatara-rust-emit")

# N0: "hi" on QEMU riscv32 virt. The emitted Rust is committed and gated
# fresh, so a change to the backend shows up as a diff to review.
generate(
  "hello-virt32",
  "images/hello-virt32.rs",
  "build/hello_virt32.b",
  ["programs/hello.b"]
)
